Z||000002||Fret Naught||06-02-2000||07:42 PM||||OH BABY BABY!!!!!<BR>Whip me beat me make me write bad checks!!!!<BR>SWEEEEEEEEET<BR>What did the engine come from?||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||06-02-2000||08:51 PM||||See you got one of them High Tech sure grip filters  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Man it looks right home in there.<BR>Cooter, what did it come out of?<BR>Next we want to know how much faster is it than the 2.8 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000004||DiggityDan||06-02-2000||09:45 PM||||I was wondering about something. When you do the 3.4 swap, do you use everything from the 2.8 - such as sensors, wiring harness and stuff like that. Also, what about oil pan and flywheel. My motor is having problems and I am looking into engine conversions. I have found a cheap enough 3800 SC that needs work but its going to cost alot to get that motor in there. How much are you out total with the 3.4?<BR>TIA<BR>Dan||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||06-02-2000||10:40 PM||||The motor is from a 95 Camaro, I gave $250 for it. All the external goodies are from the Fiero's 2.8- it is in an 88, so I used the flywheel from the original motor (internally balanced). The fuel injectors from the 3.4 are used in the Fiero fuel rail. All the sensors and engine wiring harness are from the Fiero. I had to buy a new oil pump because the pickup tube for the 3.4's oil pan hit the Fiero pan. I bought a stock replacement instead of a high volume and it still holds 80 PSI of oil pressure at idle! I tried using the old pick up tube from the 2.8 in the 3.4's pump but the tubing size was different. I cant drive the car yet becasue I dont have a correct slave cylinder for the 4.10 geared four speed or a shift cable, but those pieces should be here by Wednesday of next week.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DiggityDan||06-02-2000||11:07 PM||||What's the horsepower figures for the 3.4? Also, will the high performance cams and stuff like that from the 2.8 work for the 3.4? anyother special tricks that you have to watch out for? I want to be able to keep my AC,is it possible with this conversion?<BR>TIA again||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||06-02-2000||11:39 PM||||A 3.4 with a 4.10?!<BR>Jeez, you're gonna be able to stand it up on its back bumper! <BR>Have any clearance problems with the Camaro manifolds?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cooter||06-03-2000||12:22 AM||||The 3.4 is supposed to use the same cam and valve train as the 2.8, so I guess the performance cams for the 2.8 would work. GM Performance parts has a roller cam for the 3.4, but it was cost prohibitive for me. The A/C will fit and I will have it soon, my new compressor has not arrived yet (thanks to Carparts.com, I have no A/C or clutch cylinder)<BR>The Camaro manifolds require a custom exhaust system because the stock Y-pipe will not come close to fitting them. The rear manifold is no problem, but the one on the front side of the engine caused a few problems. The engine wiring harness is pretty close to it, so I w double wrapped the harness in insulation and then stainless duct tape. The coolant cross over pipe that bolts on the front side of the engine will not fit. I cut the upper end of the coolant pipe off where it makes the 90 degree bend and used a slightly longer upper hose and a flexable lower hose. Now the pipe is suspended between the engine and firewall by the hoses and a couple of wire ties.||||reg||1
Z||000009||bHooper||06-03-2000||08:37 AM||||Damn, Cooter!  I like... I like!<P>Question... why did you chose the 4 spd?  I thought you had a couple of 5's laying around?<P>Where did you get your 3.4?  Local salvage yard?... or a more national place that we all can take advantage of?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Enjoy!!<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000010||Cooter||06-03-2000||06:58 PM||||I have 2 Isuzu trannys, just in case I dont like the 4 speed. The reason for the low geared 4 speed is my daily commute to work. Several miles of 1 red light per block driving. I never get out of 3rd gear and usually lug the engine pretty bad climbing the hills. <P>The engine was from a local salvage yard. The reason for the good price was the yard's owner had just sold several cars to a large dismantler and they would not miss one engine from a wrecked car. Lucky me!<P>BTW- Got the car back from the muffler shop today. True duals, but only 2 inch pipe. The mufflers are "turbo tubes". They look like big glass packs. As soon as I get my clutch cylinder and can get the car back on the lift, I will post more pictures of the exhaust system.<p>[This message has been edited by Cooter (edited 06-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Cooter||06-06-2000||10:30 PM||||Got the new clutch master and slave cylinders today along with 2 new shifter cables.<P>The Demon actually moved under its own power today!!!! DAMN!!!!!!! This thing rocks! Step on the throttle in first gear and it will break the tires loose easily! (235/60's)<BR>Granny shift into second and it will chirp the tires, stand on the throttle and when it gets to about 3,000 RPM's it starts spinning the tires again.<P>I LIKE IT!!!!! Engine pulls strong to the redline, but torque steer is pretty bad. ||||reg||1
